<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- RUST_CATHEDRAL_MECHANICS_1 §2, Tier 2 resource. ParentName="ResourceBase"
       (same parent Steel/RUT_FungalSoil/RUT_CathedralRoachShell use).

       ❓ DECIDED AT BUILD (the kit spec's own open question — "stuff-capable
       ❓ — decide at build whether it is a trade commodity only or a
       buildable stuff; the sheet only requires 'distinctly valuable'"):

       TRADE-COMMODITY ONLY, NOT STUFF-CAPABLE, this pass. Reasoning:
       - "Distinctly valuable" is fully satisfied by MarketValue 8 (~4x
         Steel's 1.9) and by supply being hard-capped per map (fixed vein
         count x mineableYield 25, no craft recipe — same anti-exponential
         floor RUT_FungalSoil's header describes) without needing a second,
         larger design surface.
       - Stuff-capability is its own commitment: stuffProps.categories,
         commonality, constructEffect, a color, and — because this is a
         WEAPON/ARMOR-GRADE alloy by implication — StuffPower_Armor_*/
         StuffPower_Insulation_* balance numbers the kit spec names no
         target for. Inventing those now risks a second silent "invented
         parameter" nobody asked for, on an S-effort item whose own build
         order note calls it the first, cheapest buildable step.
       - Nothing about §P's "defunct alloy" register requires it to be
         buildable; a trade good that funds the colony is exactly what
         Tier 2's player experience line asks for ("seams of dead
         smartsteel worth real trade").
       - Reversible: stuffCategories/stuffProps can be added later in a
         content pass without touching this def's identity or any existing
         save, if a future sitting wants smartsteel gear.

       PLACEHOLDER ART: reuses vanilla Steel's own item icon, tinted, same
       "confirmed-real path, not invented" placeholder move RUT_FungalSoil
       and RUT_CathedralRoachShell both use. Real bespoke item art is owed. -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RUT_DeadSmartsteel</defName>
    <label>dead smartsteel</label>
    <description>A dense, oddly patterned alloy pulled from the walls of the plateau. It was smart once — self-assembling, self-repairing — and now it is just very good metal, still worth real money to anyone who deals in the strange.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/Steel</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <color>(150,145,168)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>8</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.5</Mass>
      <Beauty>-2</Beauty>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
    <resourceReadoutPriority>Middle</resourceReadoutPriority>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>ExoticMisc</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
